## 5. Greenfield & Reference Architecture Research Protocol (Mode F)

When the user presents an architecture idea, asks to design/create a new application (e.g., *Uber / Ola Ride-Hailing*, *Netflix Streaming*, *Slack Real-Time Chat*, *Shopify E-Commerce*, *Stripe Payment Engine*), or requests industry benchmarking against market leaders:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    REQ["User: 'Create an app like Uber/Ola' or Idea"] --> SCOPE["Orchestrator: Market Domain Triage\n(Vertical: Real-Time Ride Hailing & Dispatch)"]
    SCOPE --> WEB["Phase 1: Deep Web Research & Market Intelligence\n- Search market leaders: Uber, Ola, Lyft, Grab\n- Study engineering blogs, whitepapers & system designs"]
    WEB --> DECON["Phase 2: The Three Pillars Deconstruction\n1. WHAT they used (tech, components, protocols)\n2. WHY they used it (latency, throughput, race conditions)\n3. HOW to implement it (geospatial cells, state machines, sagas)"]
    DECON --> STACK["Phase 3: repo-analyst (Market Tech Selection)\n- Recommend production runtime, database, messaging\n- Output: reponix/market-research.md"]
    STACK --> ARCH["Phase 4: arch-mapper (Reference Blueprint & Diagrams)\n- Map Ingress, FastPath, Event Streaming, Storage tiers\n- Visual Mermaid topologies & end-to-end sequence flows\n- Output: reponix/reference-architecture.md"]
    ARCH --> SPEC["Phase 5: modernizer (Bulletproof Implementation Spec)\n- Target-neutral OpenAPI/AsyncAPI contracts, FSM models\n- Distributed mutex, idempotency, retry & DLQ resilience\n- Phased MVP-to-scale implementation roadmap\n- Output: reponix/reconstruction-spec.md"]
    SPEC --> AUDIT["Phase 6: validator (Industry Fitness & Resilience Audit)\n- Audit edge cases, network partitions, double-booking safety\n- Output: reponix/validation-report.md"]
    AUDIT --> DELIVER["Delivery: reponix/ & Executive Briefing\nBulletproof, production-grade industry blueprint!"]
```

### The Three Pillars Research Methodology:
1. **WHAT They Used:** Catalog production technologies, architectural patterns, and protocols adopted by market leaders.
2. **WHY They Used It:** Document concrete operational, latency, and throughput bottlenecks driving each choice.
3. **HOW to Implement This:** Define exact implementation mechanics: geospatial partitioning, state machines, sagas, distributed mutex, idempotency, and DLQs.

