## 7. Token Budgeting & Artifact Chunking Guardrails

To prevent LLM context truncation or lost details in large codebases:
1. **Single File Threshold:** If any generated artifact (`contracts.md`, `reconstruction-spec.md`, `architecture.md`) exceeds **600 lines** or covers more than **4 distinct domain modules**, split the artifact into modular subdocuments:
   - `reponix/reconstruction-spec/README.md` (Master index and architecture scaffold)
   - `reponix/reconstruction-spec/domain-<module>.md` (Domain rules & algorithmic pseudo-code per module)
   - `reponix/reconstruction-spec/persistence.md` (Full database DDL and indexes)
   - `reponix/reconstruction-spec/contracts.md` (OpenAPI and AsyncAPI schemas)
   - `reponix/reconstruction-spec/runbook.md` (Phased implementation prompts)
2. **Never Truncate Code Blocks:** Never use `// ... remaining code` or `/* repeat for other fields */`. Emit complete, compilable definitions. If a section is large, write it to a dedicated subfile.

